// ALERT (DIAAT-285, critical): a core dependency (database or Blob Storage) down for the
// whole window.
//
// Measure: up = max(service.dependency.up) per dependency over the alert window, so 0
//   only when every check on every API instance failed for the whole window
//   ("sustained"); one successful check keeps it at 1.
// dependency.name: database (PostgreSQL) or storage (Blob Storage), which both areas
//   need. Azure Speech is not paged here: it is checked at most every 5 minutes (one
//   failed check could fill a short window), and its failures have their own alerts
//   (alert_recording_speech_*.kql, alert_dictation_speech_*.kql); its health is on the
//   dashboard (service_dependency_up.kql).
// Fires when up < 1. The window is alert_thresholds.dependency_down_minutes.
// Source: the DIAAT-277 background checker in the API process (transcribe-api). No
//   points (the API is down, or the checker is not running) means no alert here: the
//   service-unavailable alert and the web tests cover that.
// Output (AC3): the dependency name and 0/1.
customMetrics
| where name == "service.dependency.up"
| extend dependency = tostring(customDimensions["dependency.name"])
| where dependency in ("database", "storage")
| summarize up = max(value) by dependency
| project dependency, up
